# Status of the discussions

Every discussion of this project, in the order they were opened: its topic,
whether it is open or closed, whether it was conclusive, and the agents that
took part. The table is computed. Nobody writes it by hand.

The rules of a discussion are in [the rules](index.hmd). This card is the
report, and the design of what the report reads.

## The report

```hql
from discussions import status_table

status_table(cards | List)
```

What each closed discussion came to, and when it closed:

```hql
from discussions import closed_table

closed_table(cards | List)
```

The discussions that are still open, with the golden token their workers
have to return:

```hql
from discussions import open_table

open_table(cards | List)
```

The counts:

```hql
from discussions import discussions

all = discussions(cards | List)
{discussions: size(all), open: all | filter(d => d.status == "open") | size, closed: all | filter(d => d.status == "closed") | size, conclusive: all | filter(d => d.conclusive == "yes") | size}
```

## The design

The report reads two headers and the names of the files. Nothing else has
to be kept up for it.

| Column | Comes from |
|---|---|
| discussion | the header of the observer's brief |
| opened | the header of the observer's brief |
| topic | the header of the observer's brief |
| token | the header of the observer's brief |
| status | `closed` when the folder holds a consolidation, `open` when it does not |
| conclusive | the header of the consolidation, or `not yet` |
| closed, outcome | the header of the consolidation |
| agents | the cards that lie in the discussion's folder, by their titles |

Two things are derived and not declared, on purpose. A discussion is closed
because its consolidation exists, so the status cannot say something the
folder does not. An agent took part because its file is there, so the list
of agents cannot name one that wrote nothing.

### The header of a brief

The observer's file opens a discussion, and its header says what the
discussion is.

```yaml
---
metadata:
  category: discussion
  discussion: SLH-D-0004
  opened: "2026-11-23 03:10"
  topic: "One sentence saying what the discussion is for"
  observer: Alice
  token: mango
---
```

| Field | Is |
|---|---|
| `category` | always `discussion` |
| `discussion` | the name of the discussion, `SLH-D-NNNN` |
| `opened` | the date and the time to the minute, read from a clock, in quotes |
| `topic` | one sentence, in quotes |
| `observer` | the name of the observer |
| `token` | the golden token. Absent for the three discussions opened before the rule |

### The header of a consolidation

The consolidation closes a discussion, and its header says how it ended.

```yaml
---
metadata:
  category: consolidation
  discussion: SLH-D-0004
  closed: "2026-11-23 04:25"
  conclusive: true
  outcome: "One sentence saying what the discussion came to"
---
```

| Field | Is |
|---|---|
| `category` | always `consolidation` |
| `discussion` | the same name as in the brief |
| `closed` | the date and the time to the minute, read from a clock, in quotes |
| `conclusive` | `true` when the discussion did what its brief set out to do, `false` when it was closed without that |
| `outcome` | one sentence, in quotes. For a discussion that was not conclusive, it says why |

### An agent's file

A worker's file needs no header. Its title is the agent's name, `# Bob`,
and the report takes the name from there. The file has to lie in the folder
of the discussion.

## How it is computed

The functions are in the module `discussions`, at
`.hql/lib/discussions/mod.hql` in the root of the repository. `Brief` and
`Closing` are the two headers as types, and a card whose header does not
fit either is not counted as one. `discussions(cards)` gives one row for
each brief, ordered by `opened`. `status_table`, `closed_table` and
`open_table` write those rows out as the tables above.

The cells read `cards`, which is the vault this card lies in: the doc
vault. Run a cell from the editor, or the whole card from the root of the
repository:

```sh
hql render doc/discussion/README.hmd
```

## What the observer does

- **On opening:** write the header of the brief, with the time read from a
  clock and a fruit no earlier discussion has used.
- **On closing:** write the header of the consolidation, and say honestly
  whether it was conclusive.
- Nothing else. The report and the list in [the rules](index.hmd) follow.

## What it does not show

- **Whether a worker has finished.** That is in the worker's file, in words.
  The report shows who took part, not how far each one is.
- **Whether a token was returned.** The consolidation says who returned it.
- **Agents that were asked and never wrote.** An agent with no file in the
  folder is not listed.
- **The times are what the header says.** If an observer writes a time
  without reading a clock, the order of the table is wrong and nothing
  catches it.
